<title>USA: Chancellor unit sells $200 million notes.</title>
<headline>Chancellor unit sells $200 million notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor Broadcasting Co said Wednesday its Chancellor Radio Broadcasting Co issued $200 million of 8-3/4 percent 10-year senior subordinated notes in a private placement.</p>
<p>The notes were priced at a discount to yield 8.92 percent, Chancellor said.  </p>
<p>Proceeds will be used to repay term debt under Chancellor Radio's bank credit facility, the company said.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to close on June 24.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1672))</p>
